  "domain": "spatial-computing",
  "definition": "A real-time rendering technique that fakes fine surface detail by storing perturbed surface normals in a texture and using them, rather than the interpolated geometric normals, during per-pixel lighting. Detail sculpted on a high-polygon model is baked into a tangent-space normal map applied to a low-polygon mesh, so bumps, scratches, and seams respond correctly to moving lights without adding geometry \u2014 a cornerstone of the game-asset pipeline and physically based rendering.",
